sdiv9: x / 9, for x from -999 to 999, truncated toward zero. Inline: no call.
Listed at cells 10-18, with x in cell 90.
Copy cells 10-18 to where the program needs x / 9, with each 90 changed to the program's cell for x; the program goes on with x / 9 in the accumulator.
It overwrites the accumulator; x is kept.
Size 9 cells. It runs 9 instructions, straight through.
Exact over the domain.

cell  contents   notes
 10     190      CLA 90   cells 10-18: 1112x / 10^4 by Horner's rule (digits 2, 1, 1, 1)
 11     290      ADD 90
 12     401      SFT 01
 13     290      ADD 90
 14     401      SFT 01
 15     290      ADD 90
 16     401      SFT 01
 17     290      ADD 90
 18     401      SFT 01
 90     000      data: x, the program's cell, which is kept
